   "text": {
    "L1": "Doctor Ramu learns to understand animals with help from his parrot, Mitthu.",
    "L2": "Mitthu explains that animals communicate through sounds and body movements, not words.",
    "L3": "A dog talks with its tail, while a cow can communicate with its ears.",
    "L4": "Animals trust the doctor because he understands them and can find what is wrong.",
    "L5": "We also use precise group words: a flock of birds, a herd of cows, and a swarm of bees.",
    "L6": "When we report speech, said can introduce a message, but told needs a listener after it.",
    "L7": "The myth is that told works just like said. It is wrong: we say 'He told me,' not 'He told that.'",
    "L8": "Now choose the word that completes the reporting sentence."
   },
